    "visibleText": "3D Visualization with Spatial Data for 5G Planning + Websites auto-tagging algorithm - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK 3D Visualization with Spatial Data for 5G Planning + Websites auto-tagging algorithm Posted on October 1, 2022 July 20, 2025 While Hong Kong is progressing with the next-gen 5G network (e.g. mmWave), 3D-visualization with spatial data published by HKGov’s Smart City initiative could offer a unique angle in our next-gen 5G rollout which is expected to include more dense cells with even higher throughput but weaker in coverage. We’ll demonstrate how we use Python libraries & Jupiter Notebook to facilitate such analysis. Date and Time : October 29, 2022 / 10:15-10:45 ( UTC+8 ) Language : English Speaker : Dr. Chung Ng, Mr. Alex Zhang, Mr. Ho-Wa Wong / HKT ( PCCW ) / Hong Kong Speaker Introduction Dr. Chung Ng Dr. Chung is a SVP at Group CTO Office of the HKT/PCCW Group, where he’s responsible for leading the group’s product and technology roadmap and strategic development. He also represents the group as board members of Lynx Analytics and Bindo Labs. Before HKT/PCCW, Chung contributed to the Big Data/AI strategy at Telstra as well as its international growth strategy. Prior to Telstra, Chung was an Associate Partner of Cluster Technology Limited which serves the Greater China market with professional services and solutions in high-performance computing, machine learning, big data, and public cloud. In 2008, Chung joined McKinsey & Company in the Hong Kong office. He received his DPhil in Information Engineering from the University of Oxford and held the Croucher Foundation Scholarship to work toward his research degree in wireless ad-hoc networks. Chung also received BEng and MPhil in Information Engineering from the Chinese University of Hong Kong. Mr. Alex Zhang, The Club’s Head of Data Science Alex Zhang joined HKT in March 2021 as Head of Data Science in HKT’s loyalty program and digital ventures arm, The Club. He is responsible for developing new analytic products and platforms to support The Club’s business partners within the loyalty and digital ecosystem by utilizing both telecom and partners’ data asset. Prior to joining HKT, Alex was the Associate Director of BCG GAMMA where he delivered data science projects to clients in the Greater China Region. With over 25 years of experience in Financial Services, FMCG, Retail, and e-commerce industries, Alex has held data science and analytics leadership roles at Citibank, JPMorgan Chase, OCBC, Standard Chartered Bank, and Prudential in both US and APAC. Alex received a BA of applied mathematics from City University of New York in the US. Mr. Ho-Wa Wong Ho-Wa Wong joined HKT in May 2022 as Senior Data Scientist in HKT’s loyalty program and digital ventures arm, The Club. He is responsible for end-to-end development of analytics solutions. Prior to joining HKT, Ho-Wa was a data scientist of Lane Crawford and Joyce Group where he delivered customer journey data science solutions to both internal and external parties. Ho-Wa had also been software engineer at startups and FAANG. Ho-Wa received a BEng of Computer Science from Hong Kong University of Science and Technology. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Organizers – PyCon Hong Kong 2022 ← Education Track | A Journey to be a Python Angel"
