    "visibleText": "Airflow v2 – Using Airflow to manage ETL workflows - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Airflow v2 – Using Airflow to manage ETL workflows Posted on October 1, 2022 July 20, 2025 In this talk, MJ will share his experiences of translating a traditional scripted workflow to using Airflow as a framework, and introduce some tips and common gotchas for Airflow. Date and Time : October 29, 2022 / 11:45-12:15 ( UTC+8 ) Language : English Speaker : Mr. MJ Tung / ActusRayPartners / Hong Kong Speaker Introduction Mr. MJ Tung MJ is a data engineer & quant analyst with over 10 years of experience working in the hedge fund industry. Having built data pipelines from scratch, and also having used data to analyse trading strategies to look for alpha signals, he has experience in data processing from both the engineering and the business user perspectives. MJ is currently working as a Senior Research Analyst at ActusRayPartners. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Exploration of MySQL Operator for Kubernetes in Python ← Healthy Machine Learning: From Theory to Practice"
