    "visibleText": "Healthcare by a Pythonista - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK Healthcare by a Pythonista Posted on October 1, 2022 July 20, 2025 Leverage Python for Healthcare Applications for Accelerated Data Discovery. Every Human Body is different. Similarities are in the patterns of demographic, environmental factors & habits. The need for today is to have customized Health Profiling & Diagnostics for so many chronic & complex health issues. Being a Python coder, I saw this pain point closely of lack of personalized healthcare. A broad classification system for Diagnostics sometimes leads to Side effects or reactions that cannot be predicted. Can Technology help here? This talk walks through python implementations of Health Profile Clustering, Graph Database Queries, AI applications to index Healthcare research papers on a large scale. Date and Time : October 29, 2022 / 15:45-16:15 ( UTC+8 ) Language : English Speaker : Ms. Shilpa Karkeraa / Myraa Technologies | Usha Renal Care Foundation / Singapore Speaker Introduction Ms. Shilpa Karkeraa Shilpa Karkeraa, the CEO of Myraa Technologies, HQ’d in Singapore running AI & Blockchain innovations across 7 Countries & 11 Industries. She is committed to Pay it Forward with Usha Renal Care Foundation to accelerate better Healthcare. She is the Global Top 20 Growth Fellow by Goldman Sachs. Author of Unlocking Blockchains on Azure & a passionate Global Technology Speaker. Neo4j’s Graphie Awardee for Medical Breakthroughs. She aims to bring a Billion People Social Impact with her works. Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← How Python is applying in Architecture, Engineering & Construction Industry ← Django Apps at Scale: Mistakes to Avoid"
