    "visibleText": "[PyCon HK x COSCUP 2022 Online Special Track] Introduction to Kedro – Building Data Pipeline with Python - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK [PyCon HK x COSCUP 2022 Online Special Track] Introduction to Kedro – Building Data Pipeline with Python Posted on October 30, 2022 July 20, 2025 Introduction to “kedro”, which is an open-source Python framework for creating reproducible, maintainable, and modular data science code. Kedro is an incubation-stage project of the LF AI & Data Foundation. Why it is useful and why you may want to use it as a data engineer, data scientist, or Product Manager. Date and Time : November 5, 2022 / 15:45-16:15 ( UTC+8 ) Language : English Speaker : Mr. Nok Lam Chan / QuantumBlack / Hong Kong Speaker Introduction Mr. Nok Lam Chan A former data scientist in HK, now a software engineer in London, maintainer of Kedro. 香港做左幾年data science，而家係 London 做緊 software engineer，kedro 其中一個 maintainer。 Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← [PyCon HK x COSCUP 2022 Online Special Track] Deep Learning with PyTorch: From Beginner to Research ← Schedule – PyCon HK 2022"
