    "visibleText": "What if…Python + Azure - PyCon HK Skip to content Menu PyCon HK Conference Highlights Schedule 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2020 Spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 Sponsors 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 Communities 2024 2023 2022 Booths 2024 2023 Organizers 2024 2023 2022 Volunteers 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020 Fall 2018 2017 2016 2015 PyCon HK What if…Python + Azure Posted on October 1, 2022 July 20, 2025 Python. Azure. Innovation. It’s more than a linear path. It’s a prism of endless possibilities where a single choice can branch out to limitless innovation with Python. In this session, Eason will be the mastermind to showcase different use-case scenarios of implementing Python in various industries and domains. Join him to discover the new possibilities with Azure + Python – let’s ponder the question of “what if…” together. Date and Time : October 29, 2022 / 11:00-11:30 ( UTC+8 ) Language : English Speaker : Mr. Eason Lai / Microsoft / Hong Kong Speaker Introduction Mr. Eason Lai A seasoned Principle Digital Solution Architect with over 20 years of experience in application development, cloud technologies, digital solutions, big data solutions, data analytics & science, and experiences in supporting various industries enterprises. Working experience includes multinational technology giant companies & financial institutions, Microsoft & IBM, and AIA Hong Kong & Macau. As a technical evangelist and strategist, he is very active on public speech, webinars, and contribution of technical articles, and open-source code repositories, whose topics include Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning, Data Analytics & Science, Solution Design & Best Practices with Microsoft Azure, Azure Cognitive Services, Azure Machine Learning, and Azure Databricks. Also, he mentored data analytics and science specialization courses in Coursera (Deeplearning.ai). Instagram LinkedIn Facebook Twitter YouTube Search for: Archives Archives Select Month November 2024 October 2024 September 2024 July 2024 April 2024 December 2023 October 2023 September 2023 July 2023 April 2023 November 2022 October 2022 August 2022 October 2021 September 2021 May 2021 November 2020 October 2020 September 2020 May 2020 April 2020 November 2018 October 2018 September 2018 August 2018 November 2017 October 2016 November 2015 History 2024 2023 2022 2021 2020-fall 2020-spring 2018 2017 2016 2015 ©2026 PyCon HK | Powered by SuperbThemes! ← Django Apps at Scale: Mistakes to Avoid ← Accelerate data preparation with Pandas and AWS Glue DataBrew"
